Effects for wizards

Each effect is an Object3D, which means it has an index inside vulkanRenderer.objects.

We need to know the index of the wizard object and the index of the actual effect object.

This can be created when creating the wizard objects (because is the only point where we have both the object indices).

WizardShootEffect can be then:

{
wizardObjectIndex,
objectIndex
}

Every time a wizard executes the attacking node it should:

- Enable the current wizard effect.
    - How do we find the effect of that wizard?
        - We can have another vector (wizardToShootingEffect) that stores the indices of it's effect.
        - We can just asume that the wizard effect will be exactly 1 position more in the objects array.
- Set the current animation seconds to 0.
- Wait for the animation to finish.
- Disable the effect object.
